{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/382520-how-inhuman-can-a-changeling-s-mein-be","id":382520,"title":"How Inhuman can a Changeling's Mein Be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-26T17:56:52-08:00","id":382520,"title":"How Inhuman can a Changeling's Mein Be?","content":"Hey there, I'm sorry if this seems like a stupid question! I'm INCREDIBLY new to WOD and my potential ST is running a mixed game, so I've been looking at character options. One character design i think would be REALLY fun to play would be a changeling based on a nuckelavee, at least loosely. I&quot;m not really sure what the general limit on how inhuman a character's true for can be is, though! Right now I was thinkin' of sticking with a humanoid figure with equine legs, webbed hands and no skin but I don't know if this would be too 'out there' for a changeling in context of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:14:16-08:00","id":382547,"title":"","content":"I don't recall the core book ever stating it outright, but the assumption seems to be that as long as you're humanoid in size and shape, you should be fine. The Mask smooths over most other weirdness, like having a set of antlers or magma skin. <i>Equinox Road</i> does say this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, some changelings in Arcadia appear far less human than their comrades who escape. Changelings who stand eight or nine feet tall, with four arms or nests of tendrils instead of arms are simply too inhuman to be able to return to the mortal world. Such a dramatically altered person may be rejected entirely by the mortal world. If the characters are desperately fleeing into the Hedge or using a travel token, they return to the mortal world or enter the Hedge only to find the changeling they were trying to rescue did not come with them. </div> </div> </div>The general idea, going with the context of the quote and the game's themes, I believe, is that during your escape from Arcadia your memories of humanity help reshape you back into something human-esque, even if you spent a year and a day as a giant spider, your Seeming and Kith acting as a sort of scar from your durance in Faerie. It's also suggested that as your Wyrd rises, you take on more inhuman elements to your mien, but this is by no means a consistent factor among the Lost. Your character description sounds pretty decent; not having skin might weird out anyone who can see through the Mask, but mechanically it won't have any effect unless you pick up a Frailty or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:29:53-08:00","id":382558,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the answer! I really enjoy the creepier fairy stories and playing scarier looking characters in general, so I'm not all that worried about him coming off a bit spooky to those who can see the real him. Nuckelavees are possibly my favorite mythical creature of all time so the idea of giving em a nod in a game makes me happy (though I'm not sure which TYPE of changeling would fit best; gonna do some reading).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T18:51:00-08:00","id":382590,"title":"","content":"The Wikipedia description makes me think Darkling, right off the bat. Though I could also see Ogre or even Elemental as distinct possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T19:21:39-08:00","id":382614,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, the Mien can look like anything... <i>so long as</i> mechanically it still works like a vanilla human + Seeming/Kith powers. In other words, sure, have some antlers, but unless you have the Hunterheart Kith they're purely decorative. That's the only real limitation on what a Mien can be, and thus encourages changelings who are still reasonably humanoid.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T20:33:51-08:00","id":382662,"title":"","content":"If I recall there's some implication that the higher one's Wyrd the stranger they can look/be. Certainly there are a handful of published Wyrd Evolution Merits that grant a stranger nature with higher Wyrd prerequisites. At low Wyrd you can get Lethal Mien to grow claws. At high Wyrd you can get Sublime to represent that you are so etherial and awesome that others cannot directly challenge you.<br /> <br /> When I run changeling I allow custom Wyrd Evolution Merits for players that want their characters to be really inhuman with features like wings or prehensile tales. One thing to keep in mind is that there evolutions should not replace any kiths. The way I do that is by making sure that any one of these Merits will synergies with related kiths. For example for my Wings the character has large enough wings to fly but given the weight of a human they can only do so for Stamina + Wyrd rounds. For most characters that means they can afford to go up for half the time and then need to get low enough the fall won't hurt them. For a Windwing they can fly freely and then glide down safely from any height.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:42:50-08:00","id":385279,"title":"","content":"I'd make a Nuckelevee a Darkling, but possibly take duel kith Leechfinger (to reflect a predatory nature) and the Ogre Water-Dweller. Or just make him an Ogre, less sneaky but more daylight friendly and go Water-Dweller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T19:00:40-08:00","id":385703,"title":"","content":"Can you dual-kith with kiths from two different seemings? I wasn't sure about that. If so, I'm almost tempted to make this fella an Ogre with the Water-Dweller kith and a dual kith with Blightbent, actually!<br /> <br /> As much as I also automatically went to Darkling when i was first brainstorming, I'm not sure that's actually the best option, in the end. Nuckelavees are creepy but their frightening nature comes much more from them being depicted as unstoppable beings of blight and rage than skulking creatures of the night, which, the more I think about it, sounds more in line with an Ogre seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T19:16:19-08:00","id":385714,"title":"","content":"Well depending on exacty which dual kith rules you are using, yes dual kiths from different seemings can be allowed, if the ST considers it kosher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T01:06:55-08:00","id":386058,"title":"","content":"There are two sets of rules for it, oddly enough. I recommend the &quot;2 points same Seeming 3 different seeming one&quot; as it gives options for only a tiny bit more cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}